  "title": "The app catalog grew, then got easier to navigate",
  "summary": "A growing community app catalog met more ways to use Pollen, authorize apps, and make things with the API.\n\nDozens of community apps joined the catalog on January 12, followed by 66 listings on January 13. They span creative tools, learning apps, games, bots, and developer workflows. Catalog work also recovered submitted links, removed invalid repository URLs, fixed category placement, and made app submission less fussy. Study Buzz and PolliDev were among the week's additions.\n\nThe path from Spore to Seed became clearer, with daily eligibility checks and an explanation of Dev Points. Authorization now shows requested capabilities and lets apps preselect models, a Pollen budget, expiry, and account permissions. Authorized keys can request profile, balance, and usage data; documentation and login defaults were updated to make those routes easier to use.\n\nNOWPayments crypto checkout was added alongside fiat checkout. Crypto purchases keep a separate balance, while Enter shows fiat and crypto Pollen together in its paid-balance display. Key guidance also became more consistent about how publishable keys and account Pollen work; the wording update did not change rate-limit behavior.\n\nPlay added audio generation with model-specific voice choices and a player, while fixing a balance display crash. Community chat can now connect through Enter to use your own API key for model listings, chat, images, and video, show your Pollen balance, and disconnect back to its default key.",
  "pr_count": 140,
